   "type": "heading",
   "level": 2,
   "text": "Equilibrium"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- In physics, the term **equilibrium** means: **A state of balance or stability**\n- In other words, a system in equilibrium keeps doing what it’s doing without any change"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 3,
   "text": "Conditions for equilibrium"
  },
  {
   "type": "bullets",
   "md": "- For objects in equilibrium:\n\n  - The **forces **on the object must be **balanced**\n  \n    - There must be no **resultant force**\n  - The **sum of clockwise moments **on the object must **equal **the **sum of anticlockwise moments**\n  \n    - There must be no **resultant moment**"
  },
  {
   "type": "heading",
   "level": 4,
   "text": "Examples of systems in equilibrium"
  },
  {
   "type": "figure",
   "orig_src": "https://cdn.savemyexams.com/uploads/2020/05/Equilibrium.png",
   "file": "assets/72b12da4640e-equilibrium.png",
   "alt": "Equilibrium, IGCSE & GCSE Physics revision notes",
   "caption": null
  },
  {
   "type": "paragraph",
   "md": "***When the forces and moments on an object are balanced, the object will remain in equilibrium***"
  }
 ]
